- **Merged identities:** `Dana Okafor` and `dana okafor` use two different emails but look like the same person. I merged them. Please confirm, because git treats them as two authors.
- **Still around:** Dana Okafor, Tomás Ibarra, Marcus Lindqvist and Joseph Gardi committed in 2026. Together they own roughly 100 lines. Everyone else with real code left 2018 or earlier.
- **Kenneth Reitz:** he committed in July 2024, which was the last time anyone but those four touched the repo.

**`records.py` (622 lines)**

| Author | Lines | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Kenneth Reitz | 318 | 51% | 2024 |
| Greg Troszak | 58 | 9% | 2017 (connection pooling and transactions) |
| Chad Whitacre | 39 | 6% | 2016 (`.first`, Python 3 port) |
